\"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"50dd6a07faa65d3b58db8723eec6f4a9044332ee93e15c4bd2f54b132593c19c","event_uuid":"5c7424c5-d6ca-4d74-95ff-059575463bed","position":{"commit_sha":"931210cdd551b291eebc2e2a8e929b61fb001af1","position":"1787914913581838001-5c7424c5-d6ca-4d74-95ff-059575463bed"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2717cd14f666042ac1ab48edb7972c105c1c14b5262f170d88615e8b627c8e95","event_uuid":"8592002c-b5e9-4da9-b005-583712093cb8","position":{"commit_sha":"b8f0bedb4c4f6e1674a46327f8f08be2bc04f5c5","position":"1787915225854737001-8592002c-b5e9-4da9-b005-583712093cb8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bcd4e5bd8ee2bc39015bc5216871217d3881fc838e7f70c6d33d419d1c747fbd","event_uuid":"7fd86f5e-1973-4745-acf6-6ae4322b63c0","position":{"commit_sha":"baa69eabef93ba23dddb0d13977015cc49556a78","position":"1787915235599845001-7fd86f5e-1973-4745-acf6-6ae4322b63c0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review BLOCK on three findings that are all the same excellent point, and it inverted the design.\n\nMy plan said ambient CI was the SOLE condition on the unsandboxed fail-open. That was wrong: wrap() already has a SECOND fail-open branch keyed on REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED (opt_out_enabled). So adding a new config key would have created two overlapping waiver surfaces with divergent semantics — worse than the gap it closed.\n\nThe fix is now SUBTRACTIVE: delete the CI-keyed branch and leave the existing explicit opt-out as the single waiver. Fewer branches, one documented way to disable the sandbox, and ambient CI can no longer do it.\n\nAlso recorded: _mutation.yml runs the gate on a plain ubuntu-latest runner whose kernel denies unprivileged CLONE_NEWUSER, so probe() returns None and the gate runs UNSANDBOXED via the CI branch today — while that step's comment claims 'Without it the gate fails CLOSED'. That lane must declare the waiver explicitly before the branch is removed, or it starts aborting; the comment is corrected too.","timestamp":1787908375580439001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Third BLOCK, correct: deleting only the branch would orphan _ci_environment() (its sole caller), leaving dead code whose docstring argues FOR the behaviour being removed.\n\nEnumerated the full edit set in the plan rather than discovering it mid-change: the helper and its branch in scripts/mutation_sandbox.py; five tests in tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py (three removed or inverted, two that stay meaningful); the stale CI-fallback prose in docs/local-dev-env.md; and _mutation.yml, which must declare the waiver explicitly and have its 'fails CLOSED' comment corrected. file_impact updated to those four paths.","timestamp":1787909176998510001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed as TWO changes, in that order, because one would not work.\n\n2320 (merged first): declare REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED on the mutation gate step and correct its stale 'fails CLOSED' comment. A no-op at the time — ambient CI still waived implicitly — which is exactly why it was safe to land first.\n\n2321 (merged second): delete the CI-keyed fail-open branch and its sole-purpose _ci_environment helper, invert the tests, and drop the CI-fallback prose from docs/local-dev-env.md. Net -19 lines in the source: the fix is subtractive, leaving ONE named waiver instead of adding a second knob.\n\nWhy the order was forced, learned the hard way: my first attempt (2319, abandoned) did both in one commit and the mutation gate ABORTED. The Verified lane takes the workflow DEFINITION from trusted main and the TREE from the change, so my code change took effect while my workflow declaration did not — the gate had neither a sandbox nor a waiver. That is the same definition-vs-tree skew documented for 0d22, biting in the opposite direction.\n\nRED proofs by real mutation: reinstating an ambient-CI waiver failed 5 tests; removing the named opt-out failed 2. Broad suite 15384 passed, 0 failed. CI green on 2321 with no failures.\n\nResidual, stated plainly: the mutation gate still runs UNSANDBOXED on its lane — that exposure is unchanged by this ticket. What changed is that it is now DECLARED in a reviewed file rather than inherited from an ambient variable, and a workstation with CI=1 exported no longer gets the same silent waiver. Giving that lane a real sandbox, as 0d22 did for the enforcement lane, remains the better end state.","timestamp":1787914913581838001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787892957220560001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9e3cd431-669b-4b1f-b02c-e8260539b585","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e668-b496-e264-4283"},{"link_uuid":"2f928913-a00e-4197-ba6c-55cdf394e264","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4a0d-ba3a-bf82-47a7"},{"link_uuid":"d5c9b677-7b2a-4e80-b8ca-00e1568ae832","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c923-020b-6fd0-4ded"},{"link_uuid":"1e487680-38fb-40d4-bfcb-78d867909647","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9d09-ef6b-95f8-400d"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`mutation_sandbox.wrap()` has TWO independent fail-open branches when no OS sandbox\nmechanism is available:\n\n1. **ambient `CI` truthy** — proceeds UNSANDBOXED with a warning;\n2. **`REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED=1`** — the explicit, documented opt-out.\n\nThe first is the problem. `CI` is inheritable and trivially set, so a workstation with\n`CI=1` exported — say, while debugging a CI script — silently runs mutation tests with\nno sandbox. That is the configuration the 2026-08-26 incident happened in, and nothing\nabout it is a deliberate choice by the person running the command.\n\n## Approach: remove the branch, do not add a knob\n\nThe fix is SUBTRACTIVE. Delete the `CI`-keyed branch, leaving the explicit opt-out as\nthe single waiver surface. Adding a new config key — as this ticket originally\nproposed — would create two overlapping unsandboxed-waiver surfaces with divergent\nsemantics, which is worse than the gap it closes.\n\nAfter this, disabling the sandbox requires naming `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED`,\nwhich is deliberate, greppable, and already documented.\n\n## The lane that relies on the CI branch today\n\n`.github/workflows/_mutation.yml` runs the mutation gate on a plain `ubuntu-latest`\nrunner. It installs bubblewrap, and its comment claims \"Without it the gate fails\nCLOSED\" — but those runners deny unprivileged `CLONE_NEWUSER`, so `probe()` returns\n`None` and **the gate currently runs UNSANDBOXED via the `CI` branch**. The protection\nthat comment describes does not hold there.\n\nThat lane must therefore declare the waiver explicitly before the branch is removed, or\nit will start aborting. Making it genuinely sandboxed (as `0d22-f664` did for the\nenforcement lane) is the better end state and is tracked separately — this ticket must\nnot silently convert a working lane into a failing one.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The `CI`-keyed fail-open branch is REMOVED from `wrap()`, together with its now\n      sole-purpose helper `_ci_environment()` — leaving the helper would be dead code\n      whose docstring argues FOR the behaviour just deleted. Ambient `CI` alone can no\n      longer disable the sandbox. Verified by a test asserting that with `CI` truthy, no\n      mechanism, and no opt-out, `wrap()` raises `SandboxUnavailable`.\n- [x] The tests that asserted the removed behaviour are removed or inverted, not left\n      asserting a contract that no longer exists:\n      `test_ci_runner_proceeds_unsandboxed_with_a_warning` (inverted: CI must NOT waive),\n      `test_falsey_ci_values_do_not_waive_the_sandbox` (subsumed — no CI value waives),\n      `test_the_ci_fail_open_warning_names_the_variable_and_its_value` (the warning is\n      gone with the branch). `test_workstation_still_aborts_when_no_sandbox` and\n      `test_a_working_sandbox_is_used_even_on_ci` remain meaningful and stay.\n- [x] `REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED` remains the single waiver, unchanged in name\n      and semantics. No second opt-in surface is introduced. Verified by a test that the\n      opt-out still permits an unsandboxed run and still logs at WARNING.\n- [x] `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml` sets the explicit opt-out, with a comment\n      stating that the gate runs UNSANDBOXED there and why, so the exposure is visible\n      in a reviewed file rather than implied by an ambient variable. Its stale\n      \"fails CLOSED\" comment is corrected.\n- [x] `docs/local-dev-env.md` no longer describes a CI fallback that does not exist.\n- [x] Every other lane is checked for reliance on the removed branch and shown not to\n      need it: the enforcement lane has a working `bwrap` (`0d22-f664`), macOS cells have\n      `sandbox-exec`, and the pytest cells only run `@live` tests that skip without a\n      mechanism. Verified by naming each lane and its mechanism.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- Ambient `CI` alone cannot disable the sandbox, and no new waiver surface exists.\n- The one lane that relied on it declares the waiver explicitly instead.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## Notes\n\nSplit from `baf9-eea0`, whose plan review refused a criterion claiming to require \"more\nthan ambient CI alone\" while verifying only warning text. This ticket's own first review\nthen corrected its central premise: `CI` was never the SOLE condition — the explicit\nopt-out already existed — which is what turned the fix from additive to subtractive.\nDiscovered from `e668-b496`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"delete the CI-keyed fail-open branch and its sole-purpose _ci_environment helper"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"invert or remove the tests asserting the deleted behaviour"},{"path":".github/workflows/_mutation.yml","reason":"declare the waiver explicitly and correct the stale fails-CLOSED comment"},{"path":"docs/local-dev-env.md","reason":"stop describing a CI fallback that no longer exists"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4a0d-ba3a-bf82-47a7"],["relates_to","9d09-ef6b-95f8-400d"],["relates_to","c923-020b-6fd0-4ded"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8592002c-b5e9-4da9-b005-583712093cb8","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f11d-f8fd-5860-448d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Ambient CI alone can disable the mutation sandbox","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b8733134-2580-45ad-a347-0052a9a57d86","d8feb38a-173e-4b37-b51d-92ec99d0095b","1eafc64c-76e3-468c-9876-22ad4e203f3e","a547f171-5dbf-4fa0-a152-53563b37cf04","642cc7af-0341-492c-b807-ad0062bde88b","157c1293-5f82-4fe8-9675-7bef9ffc2154","69135dd1-ef43-429f-8ade-f2aa4c39136d","bd1cf787-1cfc-450a-aafd-53746ca21e41","2f928913-a00e-4197-ba6c-55cdf394e264","d5c9b677-7b2a-4e80-b8ca-00e1568ae832","1e487680-38fb-40d4-bfcb-78d867909647","c3a1fa03-bca1-46eb-9a68-d1d4e7d8b32d","5c7424c5-d6ca-4d74-95ff-059575463bed","8592002c-b5e9-4da9-b005-583712093cb8","7fd86f5e-1973-4745-acf6-6ae4322b63c0"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787933551821948592,"uuid":"9943fd30-c0a8-4efa-b5a9-d181b872ec06"}